# Cache rules for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# The one rule that matters: index.html must never be reused from cache.
# Everything under _expo/ and assets/ is content-hashed, so a new build produces
# new filenames — but the HTML that names them keeps the same URL. If a browser
# holds an old index.html after a deploy, it asks for a bundle that no longer
# exists, the script 404s, and the page sits there with nothing on it. Reloading
# fetches the same cached HTML and fails the same way, which is why the only way
# out was closing the browser.
#
# So: HTML revalidates every time, hashed assets are immutable and cached for a
# year. That is the standard pairing and it is what makes a deploy take effect
# on the next navigation rather than whenever a cache happens to expire.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/_expo/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
